      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on two standard 6-sided dice is a prime number, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of possible outcomes when two dice are tossed:**\n   Each die has 6 faces, so the total number of outcomes is:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 6 = 36\n   \\]\n\n2. **List all possible sums of the numbers on the two dice:**\n   The smallest sum occurs when both dice show 1:\n   \\[\n   1 + 1 = 2\n   \\]\n   The largest sum occurs when both dice show 6:\n   \\[\n   6 + 6 = 12\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the possible sums range from 2 to 12. We need to identify which of these sums are prime numbers.\n\n3. **Identify the prime numbers between 2 and 12:**\n   The prime numbers in this range are:\n   \\[\n   2, 3, 5, 7, 11\n   \\]\n\n4. **Count the number of ways to achieve each prime sum:**\n   - **Sum = 2:** (1, 1) — 1 way\n   - **Sum = 3:** (1, 2), (2, 1) — 2 ways\n   - **Sum = 5:** (1, 4), (2, 3), (3, 2), (4, 1) — 4 ways\n   - **Sum = 7:** (1, 6), (2, 5), (3, 4), (4, 3), (5, 2), (6, 1) — 6 ways\n   - **Sum = 11:** (5, 6), (6, 5) — 2 ways\n\n   Adding these, the total number of ways to get a prime sum is:\n   \\[\n   1 + 2 + 4 + 6 + 2 = 15\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the probability:**\n   The probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on the dice is a prime number is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}\n\\]",
