      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on two standard 6-sided dice is a prime number, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the total number of possible outcomes when two dice are rolled.\n2. Identify all the outcomes that result in a prime number sum.\n3. Calculate the probability as the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes.\n\n### Step 1: Total Number of Outcomes\nEach die has 6 faces, so when two dice are rolled, the total number of possible outcomes is:\n\\[\n6 \\times 6 = 36\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Identify Favorable Outcomes\nWe need to find all pairs \\((a, b)\\) where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are the numbers on the two dice, and their sum \\(a + b\\) is a prime number. We will list all such pairs:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|cccccc}\n+ & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\\n\\hline\n1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 7 \\\\\n2 & 3 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 7 & 8 \\\\\n3 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 7 & 8 & 9 \\\\\n4 & 5 & 6 & 7 & 8 & 9 & 10 \\\\\n5 & 6 & 7 & 8 & 9 & 10 & 11 \\\\\n6 & 7 & 8 & 9 & 10 & 11 & 12 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nFrom the table above, we list all sums that are prime numbers:\n\\[\n2, 3, 5, 7, 11\n\\]\n\nNow, we identify the pairs that achieve these sums:\n- Sum = 2: \\((1, 1)\\)\n- Sum = 3: \\((1, 2), (2, 1)\\)\n- Sum = 5: \\((1, 4), (2, 3), (3, 2), (4, 1)\\)\n- Sum = 7: \\((1, 6), (2, 5), (3, 4), (4, 3), (5, 2), (6, 1)\\)\n- Sum = 11: \\((5, 6), (6, 5)\\)\n\nCounting these pairs, we have:\n\\[\n1 + 2 + 4 + 5 + 2 = 14 \\text{ favorable outcomes}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the Probability\nThe probability \\(P\\) that the sum of the numbers on the dice is a prime number is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes:\n\\[\nP = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable outcomes}}{\\text{Total number of outcomes}} = \\frac{14}{36}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{14}{36} = \\frac{7}{18}\n\\]\n\nThus, the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on the dice is a prime number is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{18}}\n\\]",
